<div class="home" data-pagefind-ignore>

  <section class="home-hero home-wrap">
    <h1>{{ site.description }}.</h1>
    <div class="home-prose">
      <p>We think the largest question there is deserves the scientific method. Given what we already have, how do we make life on Earth as good as it can be? Not by vibes, and not by whoever shouts loudest. By measuring what actually happens to people, and doing more of whatever works.</p>
      <p>The long-run objective is as much pleasant consciousness in the universe as possible. The near-term proxy, borrowed from the <a href="https://manual.warondisease.org/knowledge/solution/optimocracy.html">Optimocracy chapter</a> of the Earth Repair Manual, is two numbers: how many healthy years the median person gets, and how much the median person has left after tax. Everything on this site is an attempt to move those two numbers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="the-bill" class="home-wrap home-sec">
    <h2>The bill</h2>
    <div class="home-prose">
      <p>Suboptimal governance costs each of us about <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.POLITICAL_DYSFUNCTION_TAX_PER_PERSON_ANNUAL.url }}">{{ mp.POLITICAL_DYSFUNCTION_TAX_PER_PERSON_ANNUAL.formatted }}</a> a year, or <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.POLITICAL_DYSFUNCTION_TAX_PER_HOUSEHOLD_OF_FOUR_ANNUAL.url }}">{{ mp.POLITICAL_DYSFUNCTION_TAX_PER_HOUSEHOLD_OF_FOUR_ANNUAL.formatted }}</a> for a household of four. Over a lifetime it is the difference between the life we have and one in which we are <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.WISHONIA_TRAJECTORY_LIFETIME_INCOME_GAIN_PER_CAPITA.url }}">{{ mp.WISHONIA_TRAJECTORY_LIFETIME_INCOME_GAIN_PER_CAPITA.formatted }}</a> richer and the diseases never arrive.</p>
      <p>This is not a metaphor. <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.GLOBAL_ANNUAL_DEATHS_CURABLE_DISEASES.url }}">{{ mp.GLOBAL_ANNUAL_DEATHS_CURABLE_DISEASES.formatted | replace(" deaths/year", "") }}</a> people die every year of conditions with no cure, mostly because the trials that would have found one were never run. For every dollar governments spend on those trials, they spend <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.MILITARY_TO_GOVERNMENT_CLINICAL_TRIALS_SPENDING_RATIO.url }}">${{ mp.MILITARY_TO_GOVERNMENT_CLINICAL_TRIALS_SPENDING_RATIO.value | round }}</a> on the capacity for war. Nobody decided this. It is what a system does when it has no thermostat.</p>
      <p class="home-note">Every figure on this page links to its calculation in the manual, with its sources and uncertainty.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="thermostat" class="home-wrap home-sec">
    <h2>Our ovens have thermostats. Our governments do not.</h2>
    <div class="home-prose">
      <p>An oven checks the temperature and adjusts the heat. That is the entire reason dinner is edible. A government announces a policy, spends the budget, and does not check. Fifty years into <a href="/drug-war/drug-war-statistics/">the war on drugs</a>, overdose deaths are at record highs and the response has been a larger budget. Whether a policy worked is, in the technical sense, nobody's job.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="home-figure">
      <div class="home-figure-scroll">
        <svg class="home-diagram" viewBox="0 0 780 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="loops-title">
          <title id="loops-title">Two diagrams. An oven: set the temperature, heat, check with a thermometer, adjust. A government: announce a policy, spend the budget, outcomes, no sensor, no comparison, no adjustment.</title>
          <defs>
            <marker id="arrow-ink" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--color-text)"/></marker>
            <marker id="arrow-soft" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--color-text-light)"/></marker>
          </defs>

          <text class="t-side" x="20" y="34">An oven</text>
          <rect class="box" x="20" y="48" width="118" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="79" y="75" text-anchor="middle">Set 180°</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M138 70 H176" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="178" y="48" width="150" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="253" y="75" text-anchor="middle">Heating element</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M328 70 H366" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="368" y="48" width="104" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="420" y="75" text-anchor="middle">Oven</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M472 70 H510" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="512" y="48" width="104" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="564" y="75" text-anchor="middle">Dinner</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M420 92 V124 H79 V96" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <text class="t-note" x="250" y="141" text-anchor="middle">THERMOMETER: MEASURES, COMPARES TO THE SETTING, ADJUSTS</text>

          <text class="t-side" x="20" y="196">A government</text>
          <rect class="box" x="20" y="210" width="150" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="95" y="237" text-anchor="middle">Announce a policy</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M170 232 H208" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="210" y="210" width="150" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="285" y="237" text-anchor="middle">Spend the budget</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M360 232 H398" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="400" y="210" width="120" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="460" y="237" text-anchor="middle">Outcomes</text>
          <path class="wire-missing" d="M520 232 H558" marker-end="url(#arrow-soft)"/>
          <rect class="box-missing" x="560" y="210" width="56" height="44" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="588" y="238" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--color-text-light)">?</text>
          <path class="wire-missing" d="M460 254 V286 H330"/>
          <text class="t-note" x="326" y="290" text-anchor="end">NO SENSOR · NO COMPARISON · NO ADJUSTMENT</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Above, a control loop. Below, what governments do instead.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="home-prose">
      <p>The fix is not a better leader. It is a loop: a sensor that measures what happens to people, a comparison against the goal, and an adjustment. That is all a thermostat is, and it is what we are building, in public, one part at a time.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="home-figure">
      <div class="home-figure-scroll">
        <svg class="home-diagram" viewBox="0 0 780 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="loop2-title">
          <title id="loop2-title">The loop being built: the goal, the budget, the policy, outcomes, and a sensor feeding back to the goal.</title>
          <rect class="box" x="20" y="40" width="162" height="62" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="101" y="64" text-anchor="middle">The goal</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="101" y="80" text-anchor="middle">MEDIAN HEALTHY YEARS</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="101" y="93" text-anchor="middle">MEDIAN INCOME AFTER TAX</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M182 71 H218" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="220" y="40" width="152" height="62" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="296" y="64" text-anchor="middle">The budget</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="296" y="80" text-anchor="middle">WISHOCRACY</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="296" y="93" text-anchor="middle">THE 1% TREATY</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M372 71 H408" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="410" y="40" width="154" height="62" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="487" y="64" text-anchor="middle">The policy</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="487" y="80" text-anchor="middle">WHATEVER THE</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="487" y="93" text-anchor="middle">EVIDENCE SUPPORTS</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M564 71 H604" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="606" y="40" width="154" height="62" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="683" y="64" text-anchor="middle">Outcomes</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="683" y="80" text-anchor="middle">WHAT HAPPENS</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="683" y="93" text-anchor="middle">TO PEOPLE</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M683 102 V170 H612" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <rect class="box" x="270" y="140" width="340" height="62" rx="2"/>
          <text class="t" x="440" y="164" text-anchor="middle">The sensor</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="440" y="180" text-anchor="middle">DECENTRALIZED FDA · TRIALS AT ${{ mp.RECOVERY_TRIAL_COST_PER_PATIENT.value | round }} A PATIENT</text>
          <text class="t-sub" x="440" y="193" text-anchor="middle">OPTIMITRON · WHICH POLICIES ACTUALLY WORK</text>
          <path class="wire" d="M270 170 H101 V106" marker-end="url(#arrow-ink)"/>
          <text class="t-note" x="186" y="188" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:10px">MEASURE, COMPARE, ADJUST</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption>The same loop, with the parts that exist so far.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="home-prose">
      <p>The sensor is the <a href="https://dfda.earth/">Decentralized FDA</a>, which runs trials at about <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.RECOVERY_TRIAL_COST_PER_PATIENT.url }}">{{ mp.RECOVERY_TRIAL_COST_PER_PATIENT.formatted }}</a> a patient{% if mp.RECOVERY_TRIAL_COST_PER_PATIENT.ciText %} <span class="home-ci">(range {{ mp.RECOVERY_TRIAL_COST_PER_PATIENT.ciText }})</span>{% endif %} instead of <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.TRADITIONAL_PHASE3_COST_PER_PATIENT.url }}">{{ mp.TRADITIONAL_PHASE3_COST_PER_PATIENT.formatted }}</a>, so that every treatment gets tested and anyone who wants in can join, and <a href="https://optimitron.com/">Optimitron</a>, which uses the policy differences between jurisdictions to work out which policies actually improve outcomes. The comparison is <a href="https://wishocracy.warondisease.org/">Wishocracy</a>, which sets budgets by asking people two options at a time instead of asking lobbyists. The adjustment is the <a href="https://warondisease.org/">1% Treaty</a>, which moves one percent of military spending, about <a class="home-fig" href="{{ mp.TREATY_ANNUAL_FUNDING.url }}">{{ mp.TREATY_ANNUAL_FUNDING.formatted }}</a> a year, into finding out what cures what. The instructions are in <a href="https://manual.warondisease.org/">How to End War and Disease</a>, which is free.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="the-world-that-could-be" class="home-blue">
    <div class="home-wrap">
      <h2>Same species. Same technology. Same Tuesday.</h2>
      <p class="home-sub">One line of the budget moved.</p>
      <div class="home-blue-grid">
        <div class="home-prose">
          <p>Imagine the experiment has already been run. A civilization kept the same physics and the same people, and moved one percent of what it spent on the capacity for war into finding out what cures what. Trials became cheap, so they ran everywhere, all the time.</p>
          <p>Cures showed up. Cures produced public support. Support produced more funding. The loop ran for a few decades and then it was simply how things were. Aging stopped being mandatory. Depression was treated as the biology it is. Budgets were set by asking people, two options at a time, instead of by whoever hired the better lobbyist. The weapons firms pivoted to biotech and, reportedly, found the transition seamless.</p>
          <p>Suffering survived mainly in history classes, where the students did not entirely believe it.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="home-charts">
            {%- for panel in futures.panels %}
            <figure class="home-chart">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ panel.width }} {{ panel.height }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ panel.title }}: {% for s in panel.series %}{{ s.label }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}">
                <text class="title" x="{{ panel.axis.x0 }}" y="11">{{ panel.title }}</text>
                {%- for tick in panel.ticks %}
                <line class="grid" x1="{{ panel.axis.x0 }}" x2="{{ panel.axis.x1 }}" y1="{{ tick.y | round(1) }}" y2="{{ tick.y | round(1) }}"/>
                <text class="tick" x="{{ panel.axis.x0 - 6 }}" y="{{ (tick.y + 3) | round(1) }}" text-anchor="end">{{ tick.label }}</text>
                {%- endfor %}
                <line class="axis" x1="{{ panel.axis.x0 }}" x2="{{ panel.axis.x1 }}" y1="{{ panel.axis.y0 | round(1) }}" y2="{{ panel.axis.y0 | round(1) }}"/>
                {%- for yr in panel.years %}
                <text class="tick" x="{{ yr.x | round(1) }}" y="{{ (panel.axis.y0 + 16) | round(1) }}" text-anchor="{% if loop.first %}start{% else %}middle{% endif %}">{{ yr.label }}</text>
                {%- endfor %}
                {%- for s in panel.series %}
                <polyline class="line line-{{ s.kind }}" points="{{ s.points }}"/>
                <text class="end end-{{ s.kind }}" x="{{ (s.end.x + 7) | round(1) }}" y="{{ (s.end.y + 3.5) | round(1) }}">{{ s.label }}</text>
                {%- endfor %}
              </svg>
            </figure>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
          <p class="home-note" style="margin-top:0.9rem">From the manual's <a href="{{ futures.source }}">trajectory models</a>: healthy life expectancy over fifteen years and median income after tax over twenty. Income is on a log scale so all three lines fit on one page.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="home-quotes">
        <blockquote>
          <p>Our children learn about "disease" in history class. They do not believe any of it. "You mean people just felt bad? Without choosing to? And they couldn't fix it?" "They held fundraising walks." "They walked? That was the plan?"</p>
          <cite>A CUSTOMER REVIEW, PLANET KETH-7, FIVE STARS</cite>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote>
          <p>We were forty-seven years from extinction when the optimizers arrived. The only difference is we said yes. Our children do not understand how a species that invented mathematics could refuse to use it.</p>
          <cite>A CUSTOMER REVIEW, PLANET THEX-9, FIVE STARS</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>

      <p class="home-more">The long version is the <a href="https://manual.warondisease.org/knowledge/futures/wishonia.html">Wishonia chapter</a>. The mechanism is the <a href="https://manual.warondisease.org/knowledge/solution/optimocracy.html">Optimocracy chapter</a>. The <a href="https://manual.warondisease.org/knowledge/futures.html">two futures</a> are laid out side by side, and the reviews above are from the <a href="https://manual.warondisease.org/knowledge/solution/earth-optimization-services.html">Earth Optimization Services</a> chapter.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="writing" class="home-wrap home-sec">
    <div class="home-sec-row">
      <h2>From the articles</h2>
      <form class="home-search" action="/search/" method="get" role="search">
        <input type="search" name="q" placeholder="Search the articles" aria-label="Search the articles">
        <button type="submit">Search</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <div class="home-cards">
      {%- for post in collections.gallery | limit(6) %}
      {%- if post.data.title %}
      {% include "post-card.njk" %}
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="home-note" style="margin-top:1.25rem"><a href="/posts/">All {{ collections.posts | length }} articles</a>, best first. Or <a href="/empiricism-2/why-think-by-numbers/">why think by numbers at all</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="home-wrap home-sec home-end">
    <div class="home-about">
      <img class="home-avatar" src="{{ site.author.avatar }}" alt="{{ site.author.name }}" width="112" height="112">
      <div>
        <h2>Who writes this</h2>
        <p class="home-role">{{ site.author.name }}. {{ site.author.bio }}</p>
        <p>{{ site.author.bioExtended }} Built most of the loop above, and would like to hear from you, especially if you think one of the numbers is wrong. The rest of the projects are at <a href="{{ site.author.url }}">mikesinn.com</a>, the code is on <a href="{{ site.social.github }}">GitHub</a>, and the address is <a href="mailto:{{ site.author.contactEmail or site.author.email }}">{{ site.author.contactEmail or site.author.email }}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
